fswatch (macOS): never block the FSEvents callback; report drops; report a path's present state

DRAFT (T-096, O-61 (h1)), against github.com/emcrisostomo/fswatch tag 1.20.1 (97757d7).
Prototype, built and checked in a scratch directory only; not used by this configuration.
1. fswatch.cpp: records are queued and written by a separate thread, so a slow reader
   no longer blocks the monitor's callback (FSEvents then drops events).
2. fsevents_monitor.cpp: MustScanSubDirs / UserDropped / KernelDropped become an
   overflow, as the inotify and kqueue monitors report it.
3. fsevents_monitor.cpp: FSEvents accumulates a path's flags; lstat decides: a missing
   path is Removed (no Created / Updated), a present one is not Removed.

